// PARAM: --analysis interval
// The concrete value of total here is fixed at 7, so total < 100 genuinely
// holds -- but the analysis cannot establish it. Mechanism: inc's single
// FunctionEntry node is reached by two distinct call sites (inc(3) then
// inc(4)), so the D/G solver revisits it, and Apinis warrowing widens the
// entered formal's upper bound to +inf on that second visit to guarantee
// termination. The following narrowing phase recovers the lower bound
// (total is [3,+inf], not [-inf,+inf]) but not the upper one, so a bound
// like < 100 stays undecided. Widening's precision cost at a repeated call
// site, not a lost fact.
//
// 04-globals/precision/02-global_var.vimp is the same program's decidable
// half (0 < total, PROVED from the recovered lower bound); only the check
// that the widening actually costs lives here.

global total;
void inc(n) {
  total := total + n
}
void main() {
  total := 0;
  inc(3);
  inc(4);
  __voblint_check(total < 100) // UNKNOWN
}
